## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Should I call 999 or 101 if my phone is stolen?
A: Call 999 if you've been hurt, feel unsafe or the theft is happening right now. Otherwise, call 101 or report it online on your local police force's website.

### Q: Will blocking my phone's IMEI stop it working everywhere?
A: It stops the phone from working on UK networks. Stolen phones are sometimes shipped abroad, where the block may not apply, which is why it's important to also lock the phone and change your passwords.

### Q: Can I track my stolen phone myself?
A: You can see its location with Find Hub, but don't go there yourself. Give the location to the police and let them handle it.

### Q: Can CrookCatcher help me get my phone back?
A: CrookCatcher gives you evidence: a photo of the person who tried to unlock your phone, the time, and the location, sent straight to your email. You can share this with the police to help identify the thief. It doesn't guarantee your phone will be recovered, but it gives you and the police much more to go on.

